<p>
  The sheet is a <code>Y.Array</code> named <code>rows</code>. Each row is a
  <code>Y.Map</code> keyed by column, and each cell is another
  <code>Y.Map</code> with <code>value</code>, <code>bold</code>, and
  <code>fill</code>. Because those are separate keys, one person can bold a cell
  while someone else types in it, and both changes stick. If two people change
  the same key, the last write wins. A value saves when you press Enter or
  leave the cell, like in most spreadsheets.
</p>
<p>
  Sorting and column order are per window. TanStack Table keeps them locally
  and never writes them to the shared document. Sort by Owner in one window and
  by Qty in the other, then edit the same row in both.
</p>
